WEBVTT

00:00:00.420 --> 00:00:06.500
Marketing begins with a practical problem: sponsors are hard to secure before an audience exists.

00:00:06.530 --> 00:00:12.370
We will test initial acquisition with licensed quizzes and a flagship item whose usage rights are confirmed.

00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:17.123
This plan describes pre-launch tests, not current users or campaign results.

00:00:17.223 --> 00:00:23.227
We will test official announcements, fan communities, events, and flagship items as acquisition channels.

00:00:23.257 --> 00:00:28.840
We screen duplicate accounts and automation, then use human review before confirmed exclusions.

00:00:28.870 --> 00:00:35.190
We measure seed acquisition from first contact to verification and the user's first completed quiz.

00:00:35.290 --> 00:00:40.330
Only sponsor advertising questions provide points. Users do not pay for them.

00:00:40.360 --> 00:00:45.160
A correct answer gives sixty points. A wrong answer still gives thirty points.

00:00:45.190 --> 00:00:51.190
Regular anime quizzes produce competition scores, but they do not add points to the user's wallet.

00:00:51.290 --> 00:00:54.706
Each weekly league groups ten users with similar skill.

00:00:54.736 --> 00:01:00.336
We will test whether weekly rankings and new matchups improve return rates and continued participation.

00:01:00.366 --> 00:01:06.808
Cash awards are funded only by sponsor contributions. User payments and company revenue stay separate.

00:01:06.908 --> 00:01:12.492
The cel-preservation support costs three thousand yen. It includes five random commemorative pieces.

00:01:12.522 --> 00:01:19.082
The eight required pieces add no points or level. They give no tournament access, cash value, or prize.

00:01:19.112 --> 00:01:24.392
Official cards and public collection displays come only after IP licensing and rights approval.

00:01:24.492 --> 00:01:29.050
Users choose whether to share results and profiles, and who can see them.

00:01:29.080 --> 00:01:34.649
We will test whether opt-in sharing can complement paid acquisition across fan communities.

00:01:34.679 --> 00:01:39.559
We count referrals after user verification and human review of suspected abuse.

00:01:39.659 --> 00:01:43.948
Management separates sponsor award funds. Financial reporting follows each contract.

00:01:43.978 --> 00:01:49.549
Our initial revenue plan has two sources: preservation support and referral fees.

00:01:49.579 --> 00:01:55.586
Advertising fees are considered only after validation. Reports use aggregate trends, not personal histories.

00:01:55.686 --> 00:02:03.406
First funding gate: beta release and 100,000 MAU, five IP licenses, an audit firm, and a legal opinion.

00:02:03.436 --> 00:02:10.037
Second gate: public release and 250,000 MAU, plus an asset audit and break-even by end-2028.

00:02:10.067 --> 00:02:15.655
Third funding gate: 500,000 MAU, operating profit in 2029, and a lead underwriter.

00:02:15.755 --> 00:02:21.334
The service aims to acquire fans, support weekly return, and test optional sharing.

00:02:21.364 --> 00:02:25.919
We measure verification, acquisition, retention, sponsor renewal, and preservation support.

00:02:25.949 --> 00:02:31.149
The seed goal is evidence that users return after the first experience.
